The '''Confederal Institute of Statistics''' ({{langx|bl|Instituto Confederal de Stadística|link=}}, {{IPA|bl|ĩʃtiˈtutow kõfɛðeˈɾaw dɨ iʃtɐˈðistikɐ|pron}}), abbreviated '''CIS''' or '''ICS''', is the [[W:List of national and international statistical services|national statistics bureau]] of [[Balisca]]. It collects and publishes information about the [[Economy of Balisca|Baliscan economy]] and [[Demographics of Balisca|population]] and carries out the [[Census in Balisca|confederal census]]. Headquartered in [[Basilio]], a commune in the western [[Trinacria]] borough, it is the Baliscan branch of [[Costat]].

== Purpose ==
The ICS is responsible for the production and analysis of official statistics in Balisca. Its best known responsibilities include:

* Organising and publishing the confederal census.
* Producing various [[W:Index (economics)|indices]] – which are widely recognised as being of excellent quality – including an inflation index used for determining the rates of rents and the costs associated with construction.
* Costat uses ICS statistics in combination with those of other national statistical agencies to compile comparable statistics for [[COCO]] as a whole. It is also widely recognized as representing Balisca on international questions of statistics.

